<Crontab syntax details>

* * * * * command-to-execute
│ │ │ │ │
│ │ │ │ └── Day of the week (0-7) [0 and 7 = Sunday]
│ │ │ └──── Month (1-12)
│ │ └────── Day of the month (1-31)
│ └──────── Hour (0-23)
└────────── Minute (0-59)

<Special Strings in Cron>
@reboot	Run once at startup
@hourly	0 * * * *
@daily	0 0 * * *
@weekly	0 0 * * 0
@monthly	0 0 1 * *
@yearly	0 0 1 1 *

<Cron Expression Meaning>
0 9 * * *	Every day at 9:00 AM
15 18 * * *	Every day at 6:15 PM
0 */6 * * *	Every 6 hours
*/5 * * * *	Every 5 minutes
0 0 * * 0	Every Sunday at midnight

<If any case two scripts need to run after the first script successfully completed use the below systax>
45 7 * * * /bin/bash -c 'echo "--- $(date) ---"; python3 /part1.py && python3 /root/part2.py' >> /var/log/<log_file_name>.log 2>&1

< Crontab releated files path for troubleshooting purpose>
	• User cron jobs are stored in /var/spool/cron/
	• Crontab log file are stored in /var/log/cron
	• Root can manage system-wide cron jobs in /etc/crontab
	• Control access files are stored in /etc/cron.allow and /etc/cron.deny
